{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Confirmed by direct experiment against real rebar code (exp_c): UsageLimitExceeded -> LLMRunnerError, and CompletionAgentStep.run catches only UnretryableOutputError (+ a textual token-exhaustion check), so bounded recovery is unreachable on budget exhaustion — the run dies at raise_completion_workflow_failure with no verdict. Additionally: even when recovery IS reached, its evidence runs pass tool_step_limit=16 (completion_recovery.py:471), and that cutoff is 400-broken on Bedrock/Anthropic (see c827 comments) — recovery must both become reachable AND lose the empty-filter cutoff. Fix folded into c827's proposal change 4."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785953380204045001,"uuid":"386f4ad2-695f-4aaa-b81c-99f5ac271ff3"}